1207621	7540	0	{{TODO: Work on this below!}}\nSweating my way between the green fields, despite my general physical discomfort, my mind drifted back to our helper. What motivated this man, with his kind eyes and deep wrinkles, to hit on someone 25 years his junior. To do it so awkwardly? \n\nIn retrospect, it was obvious. Despite the drag shows and cabaret {{ugh}} of Paris, rural France is still very conservative and homosexuality {{more casual}} is not well tolerated. Especially for older men, the lifestyle was very much hidden. A few days earlier, also hungry, I stopped to have lunch next to a public toilet block. I was also approached by an overly-persistent man many years my senior. Living in the open was always too risky, so you find your ways around it. \n\nI think these circumstances are unfortunately especially difficult for the sensitive and empathetic souls. Who are forced into distance despite a strong need for connection. And voilà, a kind man forced into hiding. Who craves connection but rightly fears the necessary vulnerability. How could you not be, when showing your true self is met with contempt. With that much raw emotion swirling inside, it's easy to hurt others or make them uncomfortable. We've all been there, I think.\n\n
